# YeetCoach — Cursor Rules

## Project Overview
YeetCoach is a Flutter coach companion app for the YeetFit ecosystem.
Coaches use it to manage clients, assign workout and diet plans, conduct video/audio sessions, and chat with clients.
Package: com.sujin.yeetcoach
Shared Firebase backend with YeetFit (same project, same Firestore, same Auth).
Coach role: 'admin' (current); will become 'coach' after completeCoachRegistration CF is deployed and existing accounts are migrated. AppRoutes.coachRole = 'admin' until then.

## State Management
- Use GetX exclusively. No Riverpod, no Provider, no BLoC.
- Controllers extend GetxController.
- All reactive state uses .obs variables.
- Use Obx() for reactive UI, GetBuilder only when tag-scoped rebuilds are needed.
- Register controllers with Get.put() in bindings. Use Get.lazyPut() when you need multiple
  tagged instances (e.g. plan-form controllers in PlanFormBinding).
  Never instantiate controllers inside widgets.
- Tag pattern for plan controllers: 'plan-$uid-$type'   (type = PlanType.name)

## Architecture
Clean architecture with three layers:
- domain/ → entities, repository interfaces
- data/ → models (extend entities), repositories (implement interfaces), datasources (Firestore/API calls)
- presentation/ → screens, controllers (GetxController), widgets, bindings

Feature folder structure:
lib/features/<feature>/
  domain/entities/, domain/repositories/
  data/models/, data/repositories/, data/datasources/
  presentation/screens/, presentation/controllers/, presentation/widgets/, presentation/bindings/

## Design System
Light mode only. No dark mode. No glassmorphism. No Liquid Glass effects.

Colors (define in lib/core/theme/app_colors.dart):
  primary:    #1E6F5C  (teal)
  secondary:  #F5A623  (amber)
  surface:    #FFFFFF
  background: #F8F9FA
  onPrimary:  #FFFFFF
  onSurface:  #1A1A2E
  subtle:     #6B7280
  error:      #EF4444
  divider:    #E5E7EB

Typography: Google Fonts — Inter for all text.
Border radius: 12dp cards, 8dp inputs, 24dp buttons.
Elevation: cards use 1dp shadow (#0000000D), no heavy shadows.
Use .withValues(alpha: x) — never .withOpacity() (deprecated).

## Shimmer Loading
Every screen that loads async data must have a shimmer skeleton that exactly mirrors the real layout.

Base widgets in lib/core/widgets/shimmer_base.dart:
  ShimmerBase — wraps child in Shimmer.fromColors(base: #E5E7EB, highlight: #F9FAFB)
  ShimmerBox(width, height, radius) — rounded rectangle placeholder
  ShimmerCircle(size) — circular placeholder

Shimmer screens (all exist in lib/core/widgets/shimmers/):
  ClientDetailShimmer — avatar circle, two text lines, then two card boxes for stats
  PlanListShimmer — list of 4 cards: title box + subtitle box + trailing icon box
Note: client_list_shimmer.dart also exists but is dead code (the old clients list screen was removed); safe to delete.

## Firestore Collections

All collection names are constants in lib/core/constants/firestore_collections.dart:

  users                  — shared with YeetFit; auth profiles
  pending_users          — pre-approval staging
  coaches/{uid}          — coach profiles (CoachProfile); written by coach, verified fields by CF only
  clients/{uid}          — client fitness profiles (ClientProfile); written by client + coach (currentCoachId only)
  training_relationships/{id} — coach↔client pairing state (TrainingRelationship)
  plans/{planId}         — workout and diet plans (TOP-LEVEL, not user subcollections)
  chats/{chatId}         — coach↔client chat threads
  challenges/{id}        — community challenges
  calls/{callId}         — 1-to-1 coach video/audio calls
  sessions/{id}          — group training sessions
  config/{doc}           — read-only app config

### plans/{planId} schema
  trainerId, clientUid, type ('workout'|'diet'), title, description, createdAt, updatedAt
  workout → days: [{dayLabel, exercises: [{name, sets, reps?, durationMinutes?, restSeconds, notes, youtubeUrl}]}]
  diet    → meals: [{mealName, time, foods: [{name, quantity, unit, calories, protein, notes}]}]

### training_relationships/{id} schema
  coachId, clientId, coachName, clientName,
  status: 'pending'|'active'|'rejected'|'ended',
  requestedAt, acceptedAt?, endedAt?, endedBy?: 'coach'|'client'

Required composite index on training_relationships:
  coachId asc · status asc · requestedAt desc

## Domain Entities

lib/features/coach/domain/entities/coach_profile.dart
  CoachProfile: uid, name, email, profileImageUrl?, bio, specializations (unmodifiable),
    certifications (unmodifiable), isVerified, isActive, averageRating, totalClients,
    createdAt, updatedAt
  Certification: title, issuer, year
  — isVerified, averageRating, totalClients are set ONLY by Cloud Functions

lib/features/clients/domain/entities/client_profile.dart
  Enums: Gender, FitnessLevel, ActivityLevel, TrainingTime, FoodPreference
  ClientProfile: uid, name, email, profileImageUrl?, age?, heightCm?, weightKg?,
    targetWeightKg?, gender?, fitnessLevel?, activityLevel?, trainingTime?,
    primaryGoal?, foodPreferences (unmodifiable), injuries?, medicalConditions?,
    medications?, foodAllergies?, availableEquipment (unmodifiable),
    trainingDaysPerWeek?, currentCoachId?, notes?, createdAt, updatedAt

lib/features/training/domain/entities/training_relationship.dart
  Enums: RelationshipStatus {pending, active, rejected, ended}, EndedBy {coach, client}
  TrainingRelationship: id, coachId, clientId, coachName, clientName,
    status, requestedAt, acceptedAt?, endedAt?, endedBy?

lib/features/plan/domain/entities/ (existing):
  WorkoutPlan, WorkoutDay, ExerciseEntry
  DietPlan, MealEntry, FoodItem
  PlanType enum in lib/features/plan/domain/entities/plan_type.dart

All entities: @immutable, List.unmodifiable, copyWith, ==, hashCode.
Use Object.hashAll([...]) for hashCode when more than 20 fields (Object.hash limit is 20).
Never include runtimeType in ==.

## Enum Serialization
Store as .name string. Parse with firstWhere + orElse fallback.
Return null (not a fallback value) when the Firestore field is missing entirely.
Return the fallback only for unrecognized string values.

## Integer / Number Parsing
Always parse Firestore numbers with (value as num?)?.toInt() — never (value as int?).
Firestore may store integers as doubles (3.0), which throws on a direct int cast.

## Key Repositories / Datasources

lib/features/coach/
  domain/repositories/i_coach_repository.dart
  data/datasources/firestore_coach_service.dart
  data/repositories/coach_repository.dart

lib/features/clients/
  domain/repositories/i_client_profile_repository.dart    (watchCoachClients, watchClient, etc.)
  data/datasources/firestore_client_profile_service.dart
  data/repositories/client_profile_repository.dart

lib/features/training/
  domain/repositories/i_training_repository.dart
    — acceptRequest and endRelationship use WriteBatch (relationship + clients/{id} are atomic)
  data/datasources/firestore_training_service.dart
  data/repositories/training_repository.dart

lib/features/plan/
  data/datasources/firestore_plan_service.dart
    — watchWorkoutPlans / watchDietPlans query plans/ by clientUid + trainerId + type
  domain/repositories/plan_repository.dart       (interface)
  data/repositories/plan_repository_impl.dart    (implementation)

## Controllers

lib/features/auth/presentation/controllers/auth_controller.dart
  — isOnboardingComplete: Rx<bool?> (null=pending, true=done, false=incomplete)
  — _routeAfterAuth(uid): checks coaches/{uid} existence, sets flag, navigates
  — markOnboardingComplete(): called by OnboardingController before navigating to /home
  — Google login: uses google_sign_in v7 API (initialize + authenticate, idToken only)

lib/features/auth/presentation/controllers/onboarding_controller.dart
  — 3-step onboarding: basic info / specializations / certifications
  — completeOnboarding(): uploads photo to coach_profiles/{uid}/profile.jpg,
    calls completeCoachRegistration CF, calls markOnboardingComplete()

lib/features/home/presentation/controllers/coach_dashboard_controller.dart
  — pendingRequests: RxList<TrainingRelationship> (from watchPendingRequests)
  — activeClients: RxList<ClientProfile> (from watchCoachClients)
  — acceptRequest / rejectRequest with per-request processingIds: RxSet<String>

lib/features/clients/presentation/controllers/client_detail_controller.dart
  — watches clients/{uid} as a live stream
  — loaded from route arguments: {'uid': String}

lib/features/plan/presentation/controllers/plan_list_controller.dart
  — streams plans/ filtered by clientUid + trainerId + type
  — loaded from route arguments: {'uid': String, 'type': PlanType}
  — exposes deletePlan(id) with confirmation dialog in screen

lib/features/plan/presentation/controllers/workout_plan_controller.dart
  — RxList<WorkoutDay> days; methods: addDay, removeDay, updateDayLabel, reorderDays,
    addExercise, updateExercise, removeExercise
  — setupWithArguments(Map args): reads uid + existing WorkoutPlan? from args
  — savePlan(): writes to plans/{planId} — returns bool

lib/features/plan/presentation/controllers/diet_plan_controller.dart
  — RxList<MealEntry> meals; methods: addMeal, removeMeal, updateMeal,
    addFood, removeFood
  — setupWithArguments(Map args): reads uid + existing DietPlan? from args
  — savePlan(): writes to plans/{planId} — returns bool

## Navigation

Named routes in lib/core/routes/app_routes.dart.
Middleware: AuthMiddleware blocks /home routes when unauthenticated;
  also redirects to /onboarding when isOnboardingComplete == false.

Routes:
  /login
  /signup
  /onboarding          → OnboardingScreen, OnboardingBinding  (top-level, not under /home)
  /home                → CoachDashboardScreen, CoachDashboardBinding, AuthMiddleware
  /home/client-details → ClientDetailScreen, ClientDetailBinding   args: {uid: String}
  /home/plan-list      → PlanListScreen, PlanListBinding           args: {uid: String, type: PlanType}
  /home/plan-form      → PlanFormScreen, PlanFormBinding           args: {uid: String, type: PlanType, plan?: WorkoutPlan|DietPlan}
  /settings            → (to be built)

## Plan Form
PlanFormBinding uses Get.lazyPut with tag 'plan-$uid-${type.name}'.
PlanFormBinding calls setupWithArguments(args) when it creates the tagged controller.
PlanFormScreen reads uid + type from args once (initState) and finds the tagged controller — it does NOT call setupWithArguments.

## YouTube in Workout Form
No inline player. TextFormField for the YouTube URL (optional).
Validate with FormValidators.validateYouTubeUrl (lib/core/utils/form_validators.dart) — single source of truth.
  Accepts watch?v=, youtu.be/, embed/, shorts/, live/ with an 11-char video id; scheme optional.
Invalid URL: shown as the field's validator error text (not a snackbar).
Show "Open on YouTube" button when URL is non-empty; prefix https:// if no scheme before launching.
On launchUrl failure: showErrorSnackbar.
Import: url_launcher/url_launcher.dart

## Atomic Writes
acceptRequest and endRelationship use WriteBatch:
  — relationship status + clients/{clientId}.currentCoachId updated together

## Security Rules (NEVER violate)
- API keys must never be hardcoded in Dart. All secrets go through Cloud Functions.
- METERED_API_KEY: served via getCallConfig Cloud Function, cached in memory only.
- GEMINI_API_KEY: Firebase secret, only in callGemini Cloud Function.
- EDAMAM_APP_ID + EDAMAM_APP_KEY: Firebase secrets, only in searchFood Cloud Function.
- role field on users: set only via Firebase Admin SDK (Cloud Function trigger), never by the client.
- coaches/{uid}.isVerified, averageRating, totalClients: set only by Cloud Functions.
- clients/{uid}.currentCoachId: set only by coach via WriteBatch in TrainingRepository.
- Never run firebase deploy. The developer handles all Firebase deployments manually.

## Debug Logging
Never use print() or bare debugPrint(). Always use:
  logDebug('message')  →  import 'package:yeetcoach/core/utils/log_debug.dart';
Logs are stripped from release builds automatically.
Never write the assert pattern directly — always call logDebug().

## Utilities
lib/core/utils/time_ago.dart         — String timeAgo(DateTime dt) — used in dashboard + plan list
lib/core/utils/snackbar_helper.dart  — showErrorSnackbar / showSuccessSnackbar (one message each)
lib/core/constants/firestore_collections.dart — all Firestore collection name constants

## Packages Available
GetX, Firebase (core, auth, firestore, storage, messaging, functions),
shimmer, fl_chart, cached_network_image, url_launcher, image_picker,
flutter_local_notifications, timezone, flutter_timezone,
connectivity_plus, shared_preferences, showcaseview, metered_realtime, flutter_webrtc,
google_fonts, flutter_slidable, intl, uuid, google_sign_in.

NOT available (removed): youtube_player_iframe, water_drop_nav_bar, animated_text_kit, cupertino_icons.

## Walkthroughs
Use showcaseview for first-time feature walkthroughs.
Store per-user seen state in SharedPreferences with key: 'showcase_<featureName>_<uid>'.

## Cloud Functions (developer deploys manually)
completeCoachRegistration — sets role: 'coach' on users/{uid} + writes coaches/{uid} atomically
getCallConfig             — returns METERED_API_KEY to authenticated users
callGemini                — uses GEMINI_API_KEY
searchFood                — uses EDAMAM_APP_ID + EDAMAM_APP_KEY
deleteAccount             — cleans up all user data + removes calls/{callId}
